{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.trace_recursion_of_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.trace_recursion_of_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeficitRecursionReduction.lean#L50-L62","doc":"Corollary: the \"trace\" sequence `G` itself satisfies the same 2-term recursion as `Q`,\n`G_{n+1} = b^{n+1}(1 + u h²) − u h²·b·G_n` (`u = h²+2`) — a clean by-product of (I) + the\nQ-recursion, recorded because it is the form the deficit recursion is read off from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.deficit_recursion_of_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.deficit_recursion_of_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeficitRecursionReduction.lean#L33-L48","doc":"**The algebraic reduction (sorry-free).** From the Temperley–Lieb identity **(I)**\n`G_k = b^k(1+h²) − h²·Q_k` (at `n` and `n+1`) and the **2-term Q-recursion**\n`Q_{n+1} = b^{n+1}(1 + (h²+2)h²) − (h²+2)h²·b·Q_n`, the deficit obeys\n`D_{n+1} = −h²(h²+2)·D_n`. This is the field-algebra core of the ∀A Milnor deficit recursion;\nthe two hypotheses are exactly the TL facts the accompanying probe establishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeficitRecursionReduction.deficit","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeficitRecursionReduction.lean#L29-L31","doc":"The normalized trace deficit `D_k = 1 − G_k / b^k` (here `b = [2]`, `G_k = qtr(ρ(w_k))`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}